181:**Given to every position** — four settings of the data, open to all three: (1) a family name "spelt differently" differs from the other list's in at least one letter, not in capitals alone; (2) apart from those 4 family names, each of the 8 has, on both its lists, the same family name, given names and date of birth, letter for letter and in the same capitals; (3) no two different children share family name, given names and date of birth, capitals ignored; (4) each of the 8 is on exactly two lists (G-04). **What divides the positions:** where, if anywhere, the data records that two entries are one child.
